1
00:00:11,241 --> 00:00:13,994
[♪ tense music playing]

2
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:32,971
[mercenary]
No bio-signals detected inside.

3
00:00:33,472 --> 00:00:35,432
[scanner beeping]

4
00:00:35,515 --> 00:00:38,185
[♪ tense music continues]

5
00:00:54,242 --> 00:00:56,411
If Jeong Jinman is actually here…

6
00:00:57,537 --> 00:00:59,581
then I'll gouge out my other eye.

7
00:01:03,043 --> 00:01:06,755
Whether he's here or not,
we stay the course of action.

8
00:01:07,422 --> 00:01:09,591
That's the reason we lost him
in the first place.

9
00:01:13,762 --> 00:01:15,972
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

10
00:01:28,777 --> 00:01:31,738
This is where you holed up
and lived the good life, is that it?

11
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:34,074
You sly dog.

12
00:01:40,372 --> 00:01:42,124
I would bet that Jinman…

13
00:01:43,708 --> 00:01:45,919
is watching us from somewhere out there.

14
00:01:47,129 --> 00:01:48,797
[mercenary]
Secret passage found in the bathroom.

15
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,215
There's a secret passage.

16
00:01:54,636 --> 00:01:57,264
[robot feet thumping]

17
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:12,404
[device beeping]

18
00:02:14,656 --> 00:02:17,075
[devices beeping rapidly]

19
00:02:19,244 --> 00:02:20,328
Pull out now!

20
00:02:21,371 --> 00:02:23,415
[beeping speeds up]

21
00:02:25,792 --> 00:02:27,794
[♪ suspenseful music builds]

22
00:02:28,378 --> 00:02:30,130
[explosion]

23
00:02:30,213 --> 00:02:33,091
[shrapnel scatters]

24
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,681
[sighs]

25
00:02:42,350 --> 00:02:44,686
[♪ ominous music playing]

26
00:02:53,153 --> 00:02:55,822
[Jinwoo] It's bulletproof.
It won't break at this range.

27
00:02:57,157 --> 00:02:58,575
[sighs]

28
00:03:08,376 --> 00:03:09,377
Let's pull back.

29
00:03:21,932 --> 00:03:28,939
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2
STYLE
::cue()

30
00:03:32,943 --> 00:03:35,904
EPISODE 02
RECLUSE

31
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:40,033
[Jian panting]

32
00:03:40,951 --> 00:03:44,496
1 YEAR LATER

33
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:47,749
[Jinman] You can blame me for all of it.

34
00:03:50,627 --> 00:03:51,628
[sighs]

35
00:03:51,711 --> 00:03:53,672
I couldn't lose you too, Jian.

36
00:03:56,550 --> 00:03:59,511
That's why the shop was created.
To protect you.

37
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:03,056
You know, I knew
you weren't ordinary, Uncle.

38
00:04:06,643 --> 00:04:08,019
But isn't this insane?

39
00:04:09,437 --> 00:04:11,231
You're saying to protect me,

40
00:04:11,314 --> 00:04:14,025
you took money and sold guns
to mercenaries and assassins.

41
00:04:14,109 --> 00:04:15,735
You're an arms dealer, right?

42
00:04:18,905 --> 00:04:22,742
That means the weapons
that you sell to those people…

43
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,120
are used to kill, aren't they?

44
00:04:26,246 --> 00:04:27,330
[Jinman] Mm-hmm.

45
00:04:27,455 --> 00:04:29,875
This is my world, Jeong Jian.

46
00:04:31,751 --> 00:04:34,880
Where you have to kill
if you wanna stay alive.

47
00:04:35,797 --> 00:04:38,466
I did the best I could
to keep you out of danger…

48
00:04:40,844 --> 00:04:43,305
but it found you anyway,
and that's my fault.

49
00:04:43,555 --> 00:04:45,223
[scoffs]

50
00:04:46,099 --> 00:04:49,019
[shuddering breath]

51
00:04:49,644 --> 00:04:52,564
[♪ tense music playing]

52
00:04:56,192 --> 00:04:58,111
I don't need an apology anymore.

53
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,783
-Take care of yourself, Jeong Jinman.
-Listen up, Jeong Jian.

54
00:05:05,493 --> 00:05:08,538
Whatever happens,
the safest place for you is with me.

55
00:05:08,622 --> 00:05:11,583
Uncle, I don't want anything
to do with this world.

56
00:05:12,542 --> 00:05:14,294
You may not wanna hear this, but…

57
00:05:17,213 --> 00:05:18,381
[sighs]

58
00:05:19,174 --> 00:05:21,134
-you're already in it.
-But that can change.

59
00:05:22,093 --> 00:05:24,220
I thought you died
and now you're sitting here.

60
00:05:25,305 --> 00:05:27,599
None of this has anything to do with me.

61
00:05:28,683 --> 00:05:30,310
You said so yourself.

62
00:05:32,312 --> 00:05:34,606
Whatever I decide to do,
it's my choice, right?

63
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:49,579
These are yours.

64
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:54,668
Jeong Jian, from now on,
you have to make it on your own.

65
00:05:54,751 --> 00:05:56,503
SOCIAL SECURITY CARD
LEE ARIN

66
00:06:08,932 --> 00:06:11,810
[♪ tense music continues]

67
00:06:27,158 --> 00:06:28,159
[Jian] One day…

68
00:06:29,619 --> 00:06:32,664
in the future, when everything is settled…

69
00:06:34,833 --> 00:06:37,127
and I can return to a normal life…

70
00:06:42,507 --> 00:06:43,591
I'll come back.

71
00:06:45,468 --> 00:06:47,470
[panting]

72
00:06:58,106 --> 00:06:59,274
[Brother] Jeong Jian.

73
00:07:05,405 --> 00:07:08,366
Here, just in case, you should take this.
STYLE
::cue()

74
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:11,578
If anything happens,
u-use it to contact me.

75
00:07:13,997 --> 00:07:17,834
And this, this is for… security.
It should help.

76
00:07:20,837 --> 00:07:24,257
And also this bag here, just…

77
00:07:24,591 --> 00:07:27,385
Once you get somewhere safe,
open it when you're alone.

78
00:07:35,727 --> 00:07:37,228
-Hey…
-Hm?

79
00:07:37,562 --> 00:07:42,358
If you and my uncle install cameras
and bug my place, you're dead.

80
00:07:42,692 --> 00:07:46,112
Okay, okay.
I swear. I won't do that, I… I swear.

81
00:07:48,990 --> 00:07:51,117
[♪ soft music playing]

82
00:07:57,165 --> 00:07:58,458
Take care.

83
00:08:00,919 --> 00:08:03,880
Jeong Jian, you too.

84
00:08:06,257 --> 00:08:09,969
[♪ determined tense music playing]

85
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:32,534
[♪ music fades]

86
00:08:41,626 --> 00:08:43,920
[Jian panting]

87
00:08:58,268 --> 00:09:00,270
[gate rattles]

88
00:09:16,995 --> 00:09:20,498
[door lock clicks]

89
00:09:45,648 --> 00:09:49,444
[Seongjo] You gonna keep running
under the moon every night? Huh?

90
00:09:54,741 --> 00:09:56,201
Will you look at that,

91
00:09:56,284 --> 00:10:00,872
our little Jian's pretending
she can't hear me, but she does.

92
00:10:04,876 --> 00:10:07,503
[♪ ominous music playing]

93
00:10:10,173 --> 00:10:12,634
[Jian breathes shakily]

94
00:10:14,594 --> 00:10:16,512
Thanks to a certain someone,

95
00:10:16,596 --> 00:10:20,099
I've got an itch on my neck
that I can't seem to scratch.

96
00:10:20,183 --> 00:10:21,517
Can you help me?

97
00:10:22,185 --> 00:10:24,979
[♪ eerie music playing]

98
00:10:27,148 --> 00:10:28,858
-[head thumps]
-[Jian gasps]

99
00:10:36,908 --> 00:10:37,951
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

100
00:10:38,910 --> 00:10:40,912
[seagulls squawking]

101
00:10:47,585 --> 00:10:50,505
[store owner]
Come get your tofu! Fresh chilies!

102
00:10:50,588 --> 00:10:51,923
Tasty garlic!

103
00:10:52,006 --> 00:10:54,384
Get some tomatoes. Cherry tomatoes.

104
00:10:54,467 --> 00:10:56,511
Green onions. Green onions here!

105
00:10:56,594 --> 00:10:59,722
Hey, come on, what are you checking
inside the bag for, huh?

106
00:10:59,806 --> 00:11:01,849
-[sighs]
-I'm hardly making squat.

107
00:11:01,933 --> 00:11:03,142
Come here for a sec.

108
00:11:03,226 --> 00:11:06,020
Look, Grandma Pilsun
ordered shiitakes, right?

109
00:11:06,104 --> 00:11:07,855
So why'd you get
oyster mushrooms then, huh?

110
00:11:08,398 --> 00:11:11,359
Ah, Woojin, shiitake or oyster,
it's all the same.

111
00:11:11,442 --> 00:11:13,278
These are actually better for you.

112
00:11:13,361 --> 00:11:15,613
And shiitakes are so expensive now.

113
00:11:15,697 --> 00:11:18,574
What's price got to do with it?
You think Hanam-do folk can't pay?

114
00:11:19,742 --> 00:11:22,203
Last time you pulled this,
those grandmas kicked ass hard.

115
00:11:22,287 --> 00:11:23,413
You wanna go through that again?

116
00:11:25,665 --> 00:11:29,419
Keep this up and your store
will stop getting business here.

117
00:11:29,502 --> 00:11:32,880
Ah, Woojin, Woojin!
Hey, why are you doing this, man?

118
00:11:32,964 --> 00:11:34,966
We've known each other
for a while now, right?

119
00:11:35,758 --> 00:11:38,052
Hey, are you lonely?
You want me to set you up? Huh?

120
00:11:38,136 --> 00:11:39,345
[groans] Stop speaking nonsense.

121
00:11:39,429 --> 00:11:42,056
[elder 1] I mean, he's just sitting
around, waiting for who knows what.

122
00:11:43,099 --> 00:11:46,561
What's there for him to do
besides eat three meals and sleep?

123
00:11:47,395 --> 00:11:49,564
[elders laughing]

124
00:11:55,611 --> 00:11:59,615
Arin, are you in some kind of a rush?
You know you can slow down a little.

125
00:12:03,119 --> 00:12:06,080
-Hey, Arin!
-Yes?

126
00:12:09,292 --> 00:12:12,003
We're hourly, girl. Hourly, yeah?

127
00:12:12,086 --> 00:12:14,422
All of us are paid by the hour.

128
00:12:15,089 --> 00:12:17,717
We have to take it slow,
so we can make more money.

129
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,136
You can't rush everything on your own.

130
00:12:21,262 --> 00:12:22,263
Right.

131
00:12:27,727 --> 00:12:29,645
I can't tell if this girl's not listening

132
00:12:29,729 --> 00:12:32,148
or just doesn't understand
what I'm saying.

133
00:12:32,231 --> 00:12:33,983
[elder 2] All right, that's enough.

134
00:12:42,408 --> 00:12:43,993
I think I'm all finished here.

135
00:12:44,077 --> 00:12:46,746
Please take your time. I'll be going now.

136
00:12:52,168 --> 00:12:53,878
What? What did I say?

137
00:12:53,961 --> 00:12:56,923
She walks off like that,
then I'm the bad guy here, is that it?

138
00:12:57,006 --> 00:12:58,925
Has it already been a year
since that girl got here?

139
00:12:59,008 --> 00:13:01,177
It hasn't been a year yet.

140
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:04,389
It's just that I don't get along with her,
I really can't.

141
00:13:04,972 --> 00:13:08,309
And when I try to start a conversation,
she barely says a word.

142
00:13:08,393 --> 00:13:11,062
That girl!
I don't like anything about her.

143
00:13:11,145 --> 00:13:14,524
Is she still running in the middle
of the night like a bat out of hell?

144
00:13:14,607 --> 00:13:17,693
-That's what I heard.
-Come on, ladies, let it go.

145
00:13:17,777 --> 00:13:20,613
-Oh, my sonny's here. [chuckles]
-How many times I gotta say it?

146
00:13:21,906 --> 00:13:23,157
How's it going?

147
00:13:23,241 --> 00:13:26,285
Ladies, listen,
we have to include Ms. Arin

148
00:13:26,369 --> 00:13:28,413
because that makes 30 of us.

149
00:13:28,496 --> 00:13:29,664
We're getting federal support.

150
00:13:30,331 --> 00:13:32,708
They'll stop the payments to everyone
if she leaves us now.

151
00:13:33,376 --> 00:13:36,838
And young folks these days expect
to be treated with a little respect, yeah?

152
00:13:37,588 --> 00:13:41,342
It's just that we're trying really hard
with her every day.

153
00:13:41,425 --> 00:13:43,594
And why are you being mean to us for?

154
00:13:43,678 --> 00:13:46,681
She's the one with the nasty attitude,
isn't she?

155
00:13:46,764 --> 00:13:50,351
Oh, my gosh. I can't understand
why you're taking her side.

156
00:13:50,434 --> 00:13:55,022
[chuckles] Why do you think?
Woojin isn't a little boy anymore.

157
00:13:55,106 --> 00:13:56,941
He's gotta start thinking about marriage.

158
00:13:57,191 --> 00:13:58,192
-[elders laughing]
-God!

159
00:13:58,276 --> 00:14:00,611
Hey, quit trying to set us up like that.

160
00:14:00,695 --> 00:14:02,655
I've got my hands full
taking care of you all.

161
00:14:02,738 --> 00:14:04,907
I mean, marriage is the furthest thing
I can think of.

162
00:14:04,991 --> 00:14:06,242
[elder 3] Well, you should.

163
00:14:07,201 --> 00:14:09,954
-Hey, um, Mrs. Pilsun. Uh…
-Huh?

164
00:14:10,454 --> 00:14:12,874
They were out of shiitake,
so they got oyster mushrooms.

165
00:14:12,957 --> 00:14:13,958
You're kidding. What?

166
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:16,377
[Pilsun] Shiitakes and
oyster mushrooms are totally different.

167
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:17,795
That general-store fraud!

168
00:14:17,879 --> 00:14:21,090
He gets low-quality junk
and just… just pockets the cash, right?

169
00:14:21,174 --> 00:14:23,176
Don't worry about it. It's handled. Yeah?

170
00:14:23,843 --> 00:14:27,054
All right, ladies, I'll drop them off
in front of the house, okay?

171
00:14:27,138 --> 00:14:28,472
Take yours when you head home.

172
00:14:28,556 --> 00:14:30,099
-[elder 2] Yeah. Thank you.
-[elder 4] Okay, sounds good.

173
00:14:32,894 --> 00:14:36,230
Meongejeon? Still got some left.
I appreciate it, though.

174
00:14:36,314 --> 00:14:38,024
-Thank you.
-It's not meant for you.

175
00:14:38,733 --> 00:14:40,109
Take it and give it to Arin.

176
00:14:40,902 --> 00:14:43,863
I was actually thinking of giving it
to her later today,

177
00:14:43,946 --> 00:14:45,865
but the damn girl just took off like that.

178
00:14:46,574 --> 00:14:47,783
When you go to see her,

179
00:14:47,867 --> 00:14:52,496
you should give it to her real casually
and say, "Wanna sit down and eat together?

180
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:53,873
Just you and me?"

181
00:14:53,956 --> 00:14:56,209
-[elders laugh]
-Ah, forget it. Cut it out. Jeez!
STYLE
::cue()

182
00:14:56,292 --> 00:14:59,003
I really can't do this, you ladies.
I really can't!

183
00:14:59,086 --> 00:15:00,713
[elder 2] You look homeless.

184
00:15:00,796 --> 00:15:02,506
-[Woojin] I'll see you later.
-[elder 1] Okay, Romeo!

185
00:15:03,424 --> 00:15:07,011
Ms. Arin, would you like
to have some of this?

186
00:15:10,765 --> 00:15:11,891
[sighs]

187
00:15:12,558 --> 00:15:13,559
That's not it.

188
00:15:15,394 --> 00:15:18,189
Arin, Arin, I… [mumbles] I… I…

189
00:15:18,898 --> 00:15:21,609
I was wondering, have you eaten yet?

190
00:15:22,235 --> 00:15:24,445
[♪ cheeky music playing]

191
00:15:25,488 --> 00:15:26,989
Arin, I was just…

192
00:15:28,950 --> 00:15:31,369
[button clicks]

193
00:15:34,372 --> 00:15:35,373
[sighs]

194
00:15:41,462 --> 00:15:44,173
[♪ cheeky music continues]

195
00:15:50,846 --> 00:15:51,847
Are you there?

196
00:15:53,933 --> 00:15:54,934
Ms. Arin?

197
00:15:57,228 --> 00:15:58,521
You there, Ms. Arin?

198
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:02,024
Are you in there?

199
00:16:08,197 --> 00:16:09,198
What is that?

200
00:16:10,741 --> 00:16:11,742
What's going on here?

201
00:16:12,034 --> 00:16:13,369
[Jian whimpering]

202
00:16:18,207 --> 00:16:21,002
HANNIBAL: THE CONQUEROR OF ROME

203
00:16:23,337 --> 00:16:24,338
[Woojin] Ms. Arin?

204
00:16:25,923 --> 00:16:26,924
Are you home?

205
00:16:30,886 --> 00:16:32,138
[yelps]

206
00:16:32,263 --> 00:16:33,472
What was that?

207
00:16:33,556 --> 00:16:35,725
-[Woojin] Ms. Arin, are you okay?
-[gasps]

208
00:16:39,603 --> 00:16:41,188
-[snare clanks]
-Huh?

209
00:16:41,522 --> 00:16:44,859
-[whirring]
-[Woojin yelping, screaming]

210
00:16:45,234 --> 00:16:47,028
[clattering]

211
00:16:54,368 --> 00:16:56,704
[Woojin whimpering, groaning]

212
00:16:59,623 --> 00:17:02,418
[groaning in pain]

213
00:17:05,755 --> 00:17:08,132
What is this? What are you doing here?

214
00:17:10,426 --> 00:17:12,845
That's… Okay, what happened is that…

215
00:17:13,721 --> 00:17:17,016
that Granny Jeomrye told me
to take this to you.

216
00:17:20,478 --> 00:17:22,355
Uh, c-could you just…? [sighs]

217
00:17:22,813 --> 00:17:25,691
[Woojin panting]

218
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:34,784
[groans]

219
00:17:40,331 --> 00:17:42,458
I'm sorry about this.

220
00:17:43,042 --> 00:17:45,336
I shouldn't be hopping the fence
without asking.

221
00:17:50,883 --> 00:17:51,884
Can I…

222
00:17:54,845 --> 00:17:56,013
ask why it's…?

223
00:18:00,393 --> 00:18:01,477
Never mind.

224
00:18:06,190 --> 00:18:09,652
[gate opens, closes]

225
00:18:15,241 --> 00:18:16,409
[Woojin] Right on my ass.

226
00:18:17,535 --> 00:18:19,537
[♪ tense music playing]

227
00:18:34,218 --> 00:18:36,595
[keypad beeping]

228
00:18:38,431 --> 00:18:39,724
[lock clicks open]

229
00:18:44,311 --> 00:18:45,730
[lock clicks shut]

230
00:18:50,317 --> 00:18:52,319
[♪ tense music continues]
STYLE
::cue()

231
00:19:14,884 --> 00:19:15,885
[♪ music ends]

232
00:19:16,093 --> 00:19:18,095
[indistinct lively chatter]

233
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:24,727
[phone buzzing]

234
00:19:27,188 --> 00:19:28,355
DIRECTOR LEE YONGHAN
MADE CONTACT?

235
00:19:29,064 --> 00:19:31,901
-[staff] Are you Attorney Jang Inseop?
-Who's asking?

236
00:19:31,984 --> 00:19:33,611
-I'll take that.
-[Inseop] No, it's fine.

237
00:19:33,694 --> 00:19:35,988
-I'll take it, it's for me.
-Sir.

238
00:19:37,823 --> 00:19:39,533
Go ahead. This is Jang Inseop.

239
00:19:40,117 --> 00:19:41,160
[Jinman] This is Jeong Jinman.

240
00:19:42,912 --> 00:19:43,913
Yeah.

241
00:19:44,872 --> 00:19:46,415
I heard you were a man of his word,

242
00:19:46,499 --> 00:19:50,002
that's why I'm confused
you're not here at our meeting.

243
00:19:50,085 --> 00:19:52,463
[Jinman] I think we both know
you went back on your word first.

244
00:19:54,173 --> 00:19:55,174
Is that right?

245
00:19:56,258 --> 00:20:00,012
I don't understand what you mean.
I've been here since 2:30.

246
00:20:00,763 --> 00:20:01,764
[phone buzzing]

247
00:20:01,847 --> 00:20:02,848
[Jinman] Check your phone.

248
00:20:06,977 --> 00:20:08,771
KIM CHANWOO
AFFILIATION: BABYLON, MERCENARY TEAM 1

249
00:20:08,854 --> 00:20:10,815
PARK CHEOLMIN
AFFILIATION: BABYLON, MERCENARY TEAM 1

250
00:20:10,898 --> 00:20:12,817
JEONG HYEONSOO
AFFILIATION: BABYLON, MERCENARY TEAM 1

251
00:20:22,827 --> 00:20:24,995
[♪ uneasy music playing]

252
00:20:34,421 --> 00:20:36,382
[sighs] Yes. [clears throat]

253
00:20:38,217 --> 00:20:39,677
Yeah, I understand what you're saying.

254
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:44,557
However, as you know,
our employees' information is classified.

255
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:46,642
It seems that you've breached our servers.

256
00:20:47,101 --> 00:20:49,478
That's a whole other negotiation,
I'm afraid.

257
00:20:49,562 --> 00:20:50,980
[phone buzzing]

258
00:20:58,237 --> 00:20:59,864
CONFIDENTIAL

259
00:21:01,574 --> 00:21:03,534
ASSASSINATION OPERATION
OF APPOINTED PRIME MINISTER OF CAMBODIA

260
00:21:08,789 --> 00:21:10,124
Uh…

261
00:21:11,417 --> 00:21:13,586
Yes, I'm understanding exactly
what you're…

262
00:21:15,004 --> 00:21:16,922
What you're implying with this message.

263
00:21:17,006 --> 00:21:21,135
[Jinman] Once I'm convinced that Babylon
is genuinely willing to negotiate with me,

264
00:21:21,218 --> 00:21:22,636
I'll contact you again.

265
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,144
We're done. Let's head back.

266
00:21:35,858 --> 00:21:37,276
How do you think he found out?

267
00:21:38,152 --> 00:21:41,530
If I knew that,
you think I would've been flustered?

268
00:21:44,158 --> 00:21:45,159
[car beeps]

269
00:21:54,001 --> 00:21:55,002
Wait a second.

270
00:21:57,755 --> 00:21:59,173
Uh…

271
00:21:59,882 --> 00:22:02,509
-I was gonna get the car washed.
-Sir?

272
00:22:02,593 --> 00:22:06,221
You should probably take the bus back.
It'll take a while.

273
00:22:06,305 --> 00:22:08,682
No, that's fine, sir.
I can go along and keep you company.

274
00:22:08,766 --> 00:22:10,351
No, it's all right. Just go.

275
00:22:10,434 --> 00:22:12,978
-It's really fine with me.
-I said, just go on.

276
00:22:14,813 --> 00:22:16,523
Right. I'll see you back there, sir.

277
00:22:26,241 --> 00:22:27,701
[sighs]

278
00:22:45,260 --> 00:22:47,846
[♪ low tense music playing]

279
00:22:49,807 --> 00:22:50,808
[Jinman] Let's go.
STYLE
::cue()

280
00:22:52,643 --> 00:22:55,020
Where… where do you…? I mean…

281
00:22:55,104 --> 00:22:56,522
Weren't you going to the car wash?

282
00:22:58,565 --> 00:23:02,319
I didn't know agents would be there.
I swear. I wasn't briefed on it. Honestly.

283
00:23:02,403 --> 00:23:05,322
[Jinman] Yes, I'm aware.
I already know who ordered it.

284
00:23:05,990 --> 00:23:08,742
[Inseop] Even so,
you shouldn't have breached our server.

285
00:23:08,826 --> 00:23:11,704
That was the only way I could have
handled this negotiation here.

286
00:23:13,163 --> 00:23:16,709
[sighs] So, all right, why don't you
just tell me what you want.

287
00:23:16,792 --> 00:23:18,293
My conditions are simple.

288
00:23:19,128 --> 00:23:20,879
A permanent ceasefire.

289
00:23:22,715 --> 00:23:28,095
Going forward, Jeong Jian, as well
as anyone I've ever associated with,

290
00:23:28,178 --> 00:23:29,722
will now be off-limits.

291
00:23:32,141 --> 00:23:33,642
If they honor this,

292
00:23:33,726 --> 00:23:36,687
the contents of the server
will never see the light of day.

293
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:39,815
Once I'm convinced that Babylon
will keep their end of the deal…

294
00:23:40,983 --> 00:23:42,484
I will return the server.

295
00:23:43,444 --> 00:23:48,574
However, if anyone so much
as touches a hair on my niece's head,

296
00:23:48,657 --> 00:23:50,993
or if she gets even the tiniest scratch,

297
00:23:51,660 --> 00:23:54,705
Babylon's true nature will be exposed
to the world.

298
00:23:55,372 --> 00:23:58,375
If I find any suspicious men
lurking around my niece,

299
00:23:58,459 --> 00:24:01,754
or if her phone just happens
to stop working for whatever reason,

300
00:24:02,796 --> 00:24:05,174
Babylon's true nature will be made public.

301
00:24:07,426 --> 00:24:09,178
These are my non-negotiables.

302
00:24:10,471 --> 00:24:11,680
That seems straightforward,

303
00:24:11,764 --> 00:24:14,058
but I don't know
if negotiations will be possible.

304
00:24:14,141 --> 00:24:16,810
I'll make the first move
to open the conversation.

305
00:24:16,894 --> 00:24:17,936
How exactly?

306
00:24:18,020 --> 00:24:21,482
First, I will convert Murthehelp
to an indefinite shutdown state.

307
00:24:22,066 --> 00:24:24,943
I will halt all transactions
and activities

308
00:24:25,027 --> 00:24:26,612
between the codes immediately.

309
00:24:27,571 --> 00:24:28,572
I'll be watching.

310
00:24:30,532 --> 00:24:33,952
Congratulations to you and your wife
on your 15-month-old child,

311
00:24:34,036 --> 00:24:36,580
Legal Team Attorney Jang Inseop.

312
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:40,793
DEPART ON SIGNAL

313
00:24:44,671 --> 00:24:45,923
Wait, that's…

314
00:24:47,382 --> 00:24:50,094
Then, for now…

315
00:24:56,892 --> 00:24:58,185
[sighs]

316
00:24:59,728 --> 00:25:02,648
[helicopter whirs]

317
00:25:10,572 --> 00:25:12,699
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

318
00:25:26,964 --> 00:25:28,382
Jinman didn't say anything else?

319
00:25:28,465 --> 00:25:31,593
No, he just stated his terms
and disappeared quietly.

320
00:25:31,677 --> 00:25:34,513
It feels like he's got Babylon
right where he wants it.

321
00:25:34,596 --> 00:25:37,432
What should we do?
Is Jinman still an active target?

322
00:25:37,516 --> 00:25:39,476
[staff 1] …orders were to…
What are you doing here?

323
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:41,353
[security] Get the hell out of here.

324
00:25:41,436 --> 00:25:42,646
[staff 1] What are you saying?

325
00:25:42,729 --> 00:25:44,022
I said, move it!

326
00:25:44,106 --> 00:25:46,191
[security] This doesn't concern you. Move.

327
00:25:46,275 --> 00:25:48,110
Step aside. Step aside now!

328
00:25:48,193 --> 00:25:49,361
What's going on here?

329
00:26:00,539 --> 00:26:02,124
We haven't met before, have we?

330
00:26:06,461 --> 00:26:07,671
I am Kusanagi Jin.

331
00:26:08,297 --> 00:26:10,549
Regional Head of Babylon East Asia.

332
00:26:17,973 --> 00:26:19,641
Despite the name, I'm Korean.

333
00:26:19,725 --> 00:26:21,518
But I never really lived here.
STYLE
::cue()

334
00:26:30,903 --> 00:26:32,029
[immigration officer] Okay.

335
00:26:32,112 --> 00:26:33,697
IDENTITY CHECKLIST
FOR IMMIGRATION OFFICERS

336
00:26:33,780 --> 00:26:35,741
Um… Uh…

337
00:26:35,824 --> 00:26:39,203
-What time do you finish?
-In five hours.

338
00:26:39,286 --> 00:26:42,956
We will finish after and…
after five hours, we go out.

339
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:45,751
Five hours afterwards come back.
You understand?

340
00:26:45,834 --> 00:26:47,336
-Okay, yeah. Yeah.
-Okay?

341
00:26:47,419 --> 00:26:48,879
-Move, move. Move.
-Okay.

342
00:26:53,175 --> 00:26:54,176
[worker] Hey.

343
00:27:14,154 --> 00:27:16,156
-[metal clanking]
-[seagulls squawking]

344
00:27:30,963 --> 00:27:33,298
[♪ cool intriguing music playing]

345
00:27:43,976 --> 00:27:45,852
-[engine revs]
-[tires screech]

346
00:27:50,399 --> 00:27:52,401
[♪ cool intriguing music intensifies]

347
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:56,071
[♪ music stops]

348
00:27:56,154 --> 00:27:57,155
Yes.

349
00:27:58,448 --> 00:28:01,118
I'll take full responsibility
and step down.

350
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:02,202
However…

351
00:28:03,954 --> 00:28:05,414
before I resign…

352
00:28:06,915 --> 00:28:09,126
I would like to be the one to finish it.

353
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:15,215
Jeong Jinman served under me
for ten years.

354
00:28:15,298 --> 00:28:19,845
Not a single soul knows Jeong Jinman
better than I do.

355
00:28:21,346 --> 00:28:22,806
Please let me be the one--

356
00:28:22,889 --> 00:28:26,601
I believe I have already given you
more than a year

357
00:28:26,685 --> 00:28:28,270
to wrap this mess up.

358
00:28:29,354 --> 00:28:30,522
Am I wrong?

359
00:28:31,982 --> 00:28:33,275
[sighs]

360
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:36,862
It's been a year since Babylon's had
a functioning Korean branch.

361
00:28:37,446 --> 00:28:40,073
We haven't been able
to deploy any covert operations,

362
00:28:40,157 --> 00:28:42,117
officials are hesitant to use us,

363
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,661
and as a result,
revenue has been cut in half.

364
00:28:45,370 --> 00:28:46,580
[laughs]

365
00:28:46,997 --> 00:28:50,876
No matter what Jeong Jinman's notoriety
is within our circles,

366
00:28:50,959 --> 00:28:55,380
the rumor that Babylon was taken down
by a single ex-mercenary…

367
00:28:57,924 --> 00:28:59,885
Let's just say our credibility's damaged.

368
00:29:00,469 --> 00:29:01,678
If that wasn't enough,

369
00:29:01,762 --> 00:29:05,724
Babylon's top secret intel could
get leaked at any time, right?

370
00:29:07,768 --> 00:29:11,730
We gave you an entire year
to clean this matter up and you couldn't.

371
00:29:11,813 --> 00:29:14,274
That tells me everything I need to know.

372
00:29:15,192 --> 00:29:16,860
The decision's already been made.

373
00:29:17,360 --> 00:29:19,321
You're released of your duties here.

374
00:29:19,404 --> 00:29:21,281
Babylon's no longer your home.

375
00:29:21,364 --> 00:29:23,366
[♪ slow tense music playing]

376
00:29:30,957 --> 00:29:33,710
[BABYLON INTERNAL CONFIDENTIALITY
AGREEMENT]

377
00:29:35,337 --> 00:29:38,256
[security] What are you doing here?
Turn around. I said, turn arou--

378
00:29:38,340 --> 00:29:39,508
-[punches land]
-[groans]

379
00:29:39,674 --> 00:29:41,176
Hey! What the hell are you--

380
00:29:41,259 --> 00:29:42,677
[clanging]

381
00:29:43,929 --> 00:29:44,930
[body thuds]

382
00:29:47,682 --> 00:29:49,059
[groaning in pain]

383
00:29:51,144 --> 00:29:54,272
You're in someone else's country.
Don't you have any manners?

384
00:29:54,856 --> 00:29:56,483
[in Japanese] This damn country…

385
00:29:57,526 --> 00:29:59,528
gets emotional about everything.

386
00:29:59,611 --> 00:30:02,948
[in English] Say hello, Bale.
She's your direct superior.

387
00:30:03,824 --> 00:30:05,033
[Bale] What are you doing?

388
00:30:05,117 --> 00:30:06,743
Weren't you gonna get Jinman?

389
00:30:07,536 --> 00:30:09,204
And what are they doing here?

390
00:30:12,582 --> 00:30:15,043
[♪ low menacing music playing]

391
00:30:17,671 --> 00:30:19,422
And you are…

392
00:30:20,757 --> 00:30:21,758
Bale?

393
00:30:24,177 --> 00:30:27,848
Orders from above are
to capture Jeong Jinman.

394
00:30:30,142 --> 00:30:31,434
That's what I'm doing here.

395
00:30:32,352 --> 00:30:35,564
[♪ electronic music playing]

396
00:30:37,816 --> 00:30:38,817
[♪ music stops]
STYLE
::cue()

397
00:31:04,759 --> 00:31:06,636
BABYLON DIRECTOR LEE YONGHAN

398
00:31:13,560 --> 00:31:15,854
[♪ low suspenseful music playing]

399
00:31:32,204 --> 00:31:34,456
[phone buzzing]

400
00:31:37,375 --> 00:31:39,044
SON

401
00:31:41,254 --> 00:31:42,714
[coughs, clears throat]

402
00:31:45,091 --> 00:31:47,636
-Ah. Hey.
-[kid] Grandpa!

403
00:31:49,471 --> 00:31:51,806
There you are. How's my little guy, huh?

404
00:31:52,432 --> 00:31:55,268
[son] I was telling him
how I wanted to hear your voice.

405
00:31:55,477 --> 00:31:56,978
-[Yonghan laughing]
-[kid] Grandpa, when are we

406
00:31:57,062 --> 00:31:58,438
gonna play catch?

407
00:31:58,521 --> 00:32:00,440
[son] You need to brush your teeth
and get ready for bed.

408
00:32:00,523 --> 00:32:02,192
[Yonghan] All right, Sanggyu.

409
00:32:02,275 --> 00:32:03,735
-[Sanggyu] Yeah?
-It's so late.

410
00:32:03,818 --> 00:32:06,112
-[kid] No fair!
-Put him to bed already.

411
00:32:06,196 --> 00:32:07,656
-[Sanggyu] Right.
-[kid] You made a promise.

412
00:32:09,157 --> 00:32:12,202
Hey, kid.
That's what moms are like, all right?

413
00:32:13,036 --> 00:32:15,455
[Sanggyu] I already told her
we had a lot of kimchi left.

414
00:32:15,538 --> 00:32:18,583
But she won't have it,
she insists on bringing some by.

415
00:32:19,542 --> 00:32:22,337
I know it's harder for her
to make the trip these days.

416
00:32:22,420 --> 00:32:24,005
I just worry about her, that's all.

417
00:32:24,089 --> 00:32:26,299
[♪ electronic music playing
through headphones]

418
00:32:26,383 --> 00:32:27,384
Are you there?

419
00:32:29,094 --> 00:32:32,138
Listen, son, quit your complaining.

420
00:32:32,806 --> 00:32:35,016
Treat your mom well while she's around.

421
00:32:35,725 --> 00:32:38,436
That goes for your wife
and my grandson too.

422
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:40,188
[Sanggyu] Dad, is everything all right?

423
00:32:40,272 --> 00:32:41,564
Of course, everything's fine.

424
00:32:42,524 --> 00:32:43,525
See you.

425
00:32:45,902 --> 00:32:48,488
[♪ electronic music continues
through headphones]

426
00:32:59,291 --> 00:33:00,458
[thuds]

427
00:33:00,542 --> 00:33:02,627
-[gunshot]
-[♪ electronic music playing]

428
00:33:05,422 --> 00:33:06,881
-[both grunting]
-[gunshot]

429
00:33:16,558 --> 00:33:18,101
[grunts]

430
00:33:23,398 --> 00:33:25,275
[yelps, groans]

431
00:33:26,026 --> 00:33:28,069
[panting]

432
00:33:35,368 --> 00:33:37,245
[groaning]

433
00:33:39,497 --> 00:33:41,791
[panting]

434
00:33:46,087 --> 00:33:47,380
[♪ music stops]

435
00:33:47,464 --> 00:33:49,174
[breathes raggedly in shock]

436
00:33:52,093 --> 00:33:54,387
-[grunts in pain]
-[body thuds]

437
00:33:56,139 --> 00:33:58,558
[♪ electronic music continues
through headphones]

438
00:34:03,772 --> 00:34:05,148
[clanging]

439
00:34:05,774 --> 00:34:07,525
-[elevator chimes]
-[elevator door opens]

440
00:34:18,036 --> 00:34:21,081
The address is Yuseong-gu…

441
00:34:24,584 --> 00:34:27,128
[♪ electronic music playing
through headphones]

442
00:34:34,636 --> 00:34:37,097
[engine revving]

443
00:34:41,393 --> 00:34:43,812
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight…

444
00:34:43,895 --> 00:34:46,022
What the hell? We're missing a guy.

445
00:34:47,023 --> 00:34:48,024
Huh?

446
00:34:49,484 --> 00:34:50,902
Hey!

447
00:34:50,985 --> 00:34:53,780
Look. We're… There's a person missing.

448
00:34:54,489 --> 00:34:56,533
-[immigration officer] Where is he, huh?
-[navigator] That guy,

449
00:34:56,616 --> 00:34:59,577
earlier, he said he's going to toilet.

450
00:35:00,995 --> 00:35:02,789
-Maybe he shit.
-Hey!

451
00:35:02,872 --> 00:35:04,874
That's no excuse. Know what?

452
00:35:04,958 --> 00:35:07,502
-You better find him quickly and--
-Sorry, sorry, sorry. Uh…

453
00:35:07,752 --> 00:35:09,754
Toilet. Uh…

454
00:35:09,921 --> 00:35:11,047
Diarrhea.

455
00:35:11,881 --> 00:35:15,510
Korean food is too spicy.

456
00:35:20,557 --> 00:35:21,599
[beeps]

457
00:35:24,686 --> 00:35:25,854
[sighs]
STYLE
::cue()

458
00:35:34,904 --> 00:35:36,948
[phone line ringing]

459
00:35:40,994 --> 00:35:42,495
[phone buzzing]

460
00:35:43,621 --> 00:35:44,622
[chuckles]

461
00:35:45,749 --> 00:35:47,417
Mission successful.

462
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:49,127
Okay, job well done.

463
00:35:49,627 --> 00:35:51,671
Take some time off
until your next mission.

464
00:35:53,631 --> 00:35:56,384
[co-leader] I miss you. You liking Korea?

465
00:35:58,136 --> 00:35:59,179
Not at all.

466
00:35:59,971 --> 00:36:02,265
The office interior is tacky as hell.

467
00:36:03,433 --> 00:36:04,768
I need to relocate.

468
00:36:04,851 --> 00:36:06,811
[co-leader]
Okay. I'll let you get back to it.

469
00:36:07,103 --> 00:36:08,313
Mm-hmm.

470
00:36:26,414 --> 00:36:29,083
MURTHEHELP - THIS WEBSITE IS
CURRENTLY UNDER CONSTRUCTION.

471
00:36:40,678 --> 00:36:41,679
[Jian yelps]

472
00:36:46,893 --> 00:36:48,895
[seagulls squawking]

473
00:36:51,606 --> 00:36:52,774
Hey, Arin!

474
00:36:53,817 --> 00:36:56,569
Oh. Hi, aunties.

475
00:36:56,653 --> 00:36:59,280
-Are you going?
-Going where?

476
00:36:59,364 --> 00:37:00,532
[Jeomrye] What do you mean?

477
00:37:00,615 --> 00:37:04,577
Once a month, folks from the island head
to the mainland to have a feast together.

478
00:37:04,661 --> 00:37:05,662
You didn't know?

479
00:37:05,995 --> 00:37:07,080
Ah…

480
00:37:07,247 --> 00:37:11,334
We eat some tasty food,
sing songs together, play some games.

481
00:37:11,417 --> 00:37:13,419
-Come with us.
-[Pilsun] Jeez, why would youngsters

482
00:37:13,503 --> 00:37:15,463
wanna hang around
with a bunch of old folks?

483
00:37:15,547 --> 00:37:17,590
What are your plans for the day?

484
00:37:17,674 --> 00:37:20,051
My phone broke, so I was heading
to Sacheon for a new one.

485
00:37:21,886 --> 00:37:23,054
[Woojin] Hi, ladies.

486
00:37:24,639 --> 00:37:26,349
[elders] Ooh!

487
00:37:26,724 --> 00:37:27,725
Together?

488
00:37:28,935 --> 00:37:31,229
[humming merrily]

489
00:37:31,396 --> 00:37:35,817
Hey, while we're out,
have sonny here show you a good time.

490
00:37:35,900 --> 00:37:37,193
[Jeomrye] Come on. Hey, come on!

491
00:37:37,277 --> 00:37:39,696
[elder] Nothing more than hand-holding.

492
00:37:40,113 --> 00:37:44,284
It's your… first time off the island,
isn't it?

493
00:37:45,034 --> 00:37:47,036
Since you moved to Hanam-do, right?

494
00:37:47,829 --> 00:37:48,830
Yes.

495
00:37:50,123 --> 00:37:51,666
Uh, you should know,

496
00:37:51,749 --> 00:37:56,087
the Sacheon boat over there comes and goes
whenever it seemingly wants to.

497
00:37:56,671 --> 00:37:58,715
It'll stay put right there
if there's no waves at all,

498
00:37:58,798 --> 00:38:00,508
not to mention their schedule.

499
00:38:01,175 --> 00:38:02,385
Hm.

500
00:38:02,552 --> 00:38:07,432
Uh, if the ship doesn't go out
or you don't get on board, give me a call.

501
00:38:07,515 --> 00:38:08,850
I can take my boat out there.

502
00:38:11,144 --> 00:38:12,520
Uh…

503
00:38:12,854 --> 00:38:15,148
That's just what everyone around here
does already.

504
00:38:15,231 --> 00:38:18,067
It's totally fine, so please feel free
to call if you want.

505
00:38:18,484 --> 00:38:19,611
Oh.

506
00:38:19,777 --> 00:38:21,279
-That's--
-I appreciate it.

507
00:38:21,362 --> 00:38:24,532
Wait! My number's really easy. Here.

508
00:38:26,200 --> 00:38:30,163
0070-1004.

509
00:38:31,623 --> 00:38:35,585
007. Bang! 1004.
You can remember it like that.

510
00:38:37,295 --> 00:38:38,963
Yeah. Really appreciate it.

511
00:38:40,340 --> 00:38:43,301
-I better get on the boat now, so…
-Yeah.

512
00:38:44,218 --> 00:38:45,219
[Woojin] Safe travels.

513
00:38:45,678 --> 00:38:47,931
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

514
00:38:54,896 --> 00:38:55,939
You idiot.

515
00:39:10,495 --> 00:39:13,539
PHONES FOR ALL

516
00:39:16,542 --> 00:39:17,543
BUS

517
00:39:20,213 --> 00:39:22,590
[♪ gentle music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

518
00:39:28,471 --> 00:39:30,056
[lively chatter]

519
00:39:39,524 --> 00:39:40,942
[sighs]

520
00:40:03,423 --> 00:40:06,175
THAI SPECIALTY RESTAURANT

521
00:40:09,303 --> 00:40:10,805
[owner, in Thai] Welcome.

522
00:40:12,348 --> 00:40:13,641
[Jian, in English] One pad thai, please.

523
00:40:14,267 --> 00:40:15,893
[owner] Of course. This way, please.

524
00:40:23,735 --> 00:40:26,946
[♪ gentle music continues]

525
00:40:30,324 --> 00:40:33,161
[indistinct Thai chatter]

526
00:40:42,628 --> 00:40:45,006
[♪ music turns eerie]

527
00:40:48,259 --> 00:40:52,263
[in English] Jian, you're here
'cause you thought of Pasin, huh?

528
00:40:52,346 --> 00:40:53,514
Yeah.

529
00:40:54,474 --> 00:40:55,892
Oh.

530
00:40:56,684 --> 00:40:58,728
Should've taken a hatchet
to his fucking neck.

531
00:40:58,811 --> 00:40:59,854
-[door opens]
-[store bell chimes]

532
00:40:59,979 --> 00:41:01,773
-[in Thai] Hi, how have you been?
-Welcome.

533
00:41:04,233 --> 00:41:06,611
[indistinct Thai chatter]

534
00:41:10,239 --> 00:41:13,159
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

535
00:41:18,039 --> 00:41:20,041
[rain pattering]

536
00:41:57,745 --> 00:42:00,623
[both grunt]

537
00:42:00,706 --> 00:42:02,708
[♪ intense music playing]

538
00:42:03,376 --> 00:42:05,545
[in English] Who are you?
Why are you following me?

539
00:42:05,628 --> 00:42:07,588
You left your cell phone in there.

540
00:42:07,672 --> 00:42:09,340
You've been following me since the bus.

541
00:42:09,423 --> 00:42:12,385
I was gonna eat there.
My friend owns that restaurant. [grunts]

542
00:42:13,427 --> 00:42:15,555
[both panting]

543
00:42:15,638 --> 00:42:16,722
[thuds]

544
00:42:23,771 --> 00:42:26,691
[Seongjo cackling]

545
00:42:35,074 --> 00:42:36,868
Do you recall what I said that night?

546
00:42:38,161 --> 00:42:41,414
That I want to recruit you,
that I want to bring you on.

547
00:42:44,333 --> 00:42:45,710
Wow…

548
00:42:46,043 --> 00:42:47,795
You take after your uncle.

549
00:42:48,462 --> 00:42:51,174
You're a born warrior. Warrior.

550
00:42:54,594 --> 00:42:55,595
Fuck off.

551
00:42:59,307 --> 00:43:01,601
[♪ tense music playing]

552
00:43:03,644 --> 00:43:04,979
[♪ music ends]

553
00:43:14,614 --> 00:43:16,949
-[rain pattering]
-[thunder rumbling]
STYLE
::cue()

554
00:43:18,534 --> 00:43:19,535
What?

555
00:43:20,494 --> 00:43:23,372
Are you saying there's no more rides
back to Hanam-do today?

556
00:43:23,456 --> 00:43:25,333
Sorry, they've all been canceled.

557
00:43:25,416 --> 00:43:27,418
These ferries can't go out
in this weather.

558
00:43:30,129 --> 00:43:31,422
[sighs]

559
00:43:33,549 --> 00:43:36,219
[staff 1] What are you doing when you
get off? Have any plans?

560
00:43:36,302 --> 00:43:37,303
[staff 2] No, I don't.

561
00:43:38,679 --> 00:43:41,390
-[staff 1] Going straight home?
-[staff 2] I really should.

562
00:43:49,607 --> 00:43:54,195
[Woojin] Uh, if the ship doesn't go out
or you don't get onboard, give me a call.

563
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:57,740
My number's really easy. Here.

564
00:44:06,540 --> 00:44:08,834
[boat engine revving]

565
00:44:09,543 --> 00:44:12,546
WOOJIN

566
00:44:15,132 --> 00:44:16,133
[Woojin] Have you had dinner?

567
00:44:17,677 --> 00:44:18,678
What?

568
00:44:19,679 --> 00:44:20,972
Have you had dinner yet?

569
00:44:22,515 --> 00:44:24,016
I haven't. Not yet.

570
00:44:31,399 --> 00:44:34,610
Here, eat this.
You'll get sick on an empty stomach.

571
00:44:37,863 --> 00:44:40,700
That right there is
a Sacheon local delicacy.

572
00:44:40,783 --> 00:44:42,201
It even appeared on YouTube.

573
00:44:43,536 --> 00:44:44,787
It's really amazing.

574
00:44:46,706 --> 00:44:47,873
Thank you so much.

575
00:44:49,583 --> 00:44:50,751
[bottles clink]

576
00:44:53,713 --> 00:44:55,464
Have it with this, it's killer.

577
00:44:56,757 --> 00:44:59,844
[♪ gentle music playing]

578
00:45:13,816 --> 00:45:15,484
Are you gonna ask me about it?

579
00:45:16,360 --> 00:45:17,445
What?

580
00:45:18,821 --> 00:45:20,781
Why I had all that stuff in my yard.

581
00:45:23,826 --> 00:45:25,745
I mean, I would've asked if I were you.

582
00:45:30,082 --> 00:45:32,501
[Woojin] Oh. Oh, that?

583
00:45:33,919 --> 00:45:36,881
Well, everyone's got
their own circumstances in life, right?

584
00:45:37,548 --> 00:45:40,926
I figured it really wasn't my business.
I don't want to overcomplicate things.

585
00:45:42,261 --> 00:45:47,016
Anyhow, the aunties,
they don't mean anything by it either.

586
00:45:47,641 --> 00:45:49,935
They're just trying to get close to you
in their own way,

587
00:45:50,686 --> 00:45:51,812
so don't let them get to you.

588
00:45:55,441 --> 00:45:57,401
-[alarm blaring]
-[coast guard] This is the Coast Guard!

589
00:45:58,152 --> 00:46:01,906
We're conducting a contraband inspection.
Please cooperate.

590
00:46:04,367 --> 00:46:05,701
That you, Woojin?

591
00:46:06,452 --> 00:46:08,621
Stop the boat. Let me take a quick look.

592
00:46:11,374 --> 00:46:12,666
Yes, I understand.

593
00:46:15,419 --> 00:46:18,339
-[engine shuts off]
-Shit. What do I do?

594
00:46:20,925 --> 00:46:23,177
Hey, Arin. One second.

595
00:46:24,303 --> 00:46:26,597
-Could you hold this for a minute, please?
-What?

596
00:46:27,681 --> 00:46:28,682
Shit.

597
00:46:32,311 --> 00:46:33,729
[Woojin grunting]

598
00:46:38,359 --> 00:46:40,528
[strained groaning]

599
00:46:41,070 --> 00:46:43,072
-[Woojin yelps]
-[clattering]

600
00:46:44,198 --> 00:46:45,574
[gasps]

601
00:46:45,699 --> 00:46:47,701
[♪ ominous music playing]

602
00:46:49,745 --> 00:46:52,039
Shit. Shit.

603
00:47:02,883 --> 00:47:04,385
[phone buzzing]

604
00:47:04,760 --> 00:47:07,972
MURTHEHELP
WHEN CAN THE PACKAGE BE RECEIVED?

605
00:47:08,264 --> 00:47:10,850
[♪ ominous music continues]

606
00:47:12,726 --> 00:47:17,481
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

607
00:47:18,649 --> 00:47:20,443
Why is it taking so long?

608
00:47:21,861 --> 00:47:22,862
[sighs]

609
00:47:22,945 --> 00:47:26,407
Look, among all of these classified
servers, there's only three real ones.

610
00:47:26,490 --> 00:47:30,661
No, I get that, but you said
you're the one who made this.

611
00:47:32,496 --> 00:47:36,083
Hey, it's not like I created the fake ones
and put them in there, all right?

612
00:47:37,251 --> 00:47:40,129
Your Kim II Sung University degree
really ain't worth shit, is it?

613
00:47:40,212 --> 00:47:42,923
[Brother]
Sir, sir, sir, Jinman! Sir, sir, sir.

614
00:47:43,007 --> 00:47:45,885
[panting]
Here, here, here, quick, quick, quick.

615
00:47:45,968 --> 00:47:46,969
What is it?

616
00:47:49,054 --> 00:47:51,140
LOOKING FOR A PERSON
$2,000,000 DOLLAR / CASH

617
00:47:51,223 --> 00:47:52,224
NAME: JEONG JIAN

618
00:47:55,603 --> 00:47:57,605
[♪ closing theme music playing]

619
00:48:03,611 --> 00:48:05,070
BASED ON THE NOVEL
BY KANG JI YOUNG

